{title: His Steadfast Love}
{subtitle: Psalms 118:1}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm7] |
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Give thanks to [Ab]the LORD, [Bb]for he is good
His steadfast love [Ab]endures forever
[Eb]Let Israel say [Bb]it with one voice
[Eb]His steadfast love en[Ab]dures forever
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]His steadfast love [Bb]endures forever
[Cm7]His steadfast love [Ab]endures forever
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Let the house of [Bb]Aaron say it
His [Eb]steadfast love endures [Ab]forever
Let [Eb]those who fear the [Bb]LORD say it
[Cm7]His steadfast love [Ab]endures forever
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Goodness found in [Bb]the ancient way
[Ab]Love that never fades [Bb]or decays
[Eb]Say it [Bb/D]now, let the [Cm]words ring out
[Ab]Steadfast love, with[Bb]out a doubt
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]His steadfast [Bb/D]love en[Cm7]dures forever
His [Eb]steadfast love en[Ab]dures forev[Eb][Bb]er
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Give thanks, for [Cm7]he is [Abmaj7]good [Bb][Eb][Cm7][Abmaj7][Bb][Eb]
His steadfast [Ab]love endures forev[Eb][Bb]er
{end_of_verse}
